    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/theming/theme-artefacts.md#provenance-1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "The surfaces",
      "prov:value": "| artefact | what differs | where |\n|---|---|---|\n| **sticky** | the container sizes to its CONTENT, so a text region would reimpose the geometry the sticky removes | `schemas/content/landing-sticky.ts`, `.fa-sticky` |\n| **landing board** | text is composited INTO the art, so it needs `textRegion` per layout and a crop chosen by content shape | `docs/_includes/landing.html` |\n| **docs background** | the page ground, not a card — a different CSS surface and probably a different crop set | not built; bean `yj32` |\n| **navbar avatar** | the art CLIPPED to the subject in a square frame — `avatarRegion` | `<name>.json`, `bun run cat avatar:crops` |\n| **the mark** | ONE geometry, TWO inks — a scheme pair, because one ink cannot clear 3:1 on both grounds | `<name>.json` `mark` + `mark-dark`, `docs/assets/img/icons/` |",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean yj32"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/theming/theme-artefacts.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Sticky: art backs it, text does not sit IN it",
      "prov:value": "**A floating sticky keeps its theme.** `.fa-sticky-floating`'s opaque override\nis scoped to `:not([data-fa-sticky-theme])`, because the theme is a property of\nthe sticky and not of the pinned state — bean `ivfw`. That scoping is sound\nonly while every theme surface is opaque, which is why `theme-declaration`\ncarries the rule and `themes.test.ts` gates it.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean ivfw"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/theming/theme-artefacts.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Navbar avatar: the box is per-image and measured",
      "prov:value": "**Two of these were wrong twice, and both times only a render caught it.** The\nfirst pass put the library and analyst boxes on scenery. The operations box was\nsquare, in bounds, and clipped the crown off the hard hat; the owner saw it and\nsaid so. **The schema cannot see a hat.** So:"
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/theming/theme-artefacts.md#provenance-4",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "The page ground: the first paint is DARK",
      "prov:value": "The owner, 2026-09-24, verbatim:",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-24"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-24"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/theming/theme-artefacts.md#provenance-5",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "The page ground: the first paint is DARK",
      "prov:value": "1. **Decide the scheme before any stylesheet paints.** An inline, render-\n   blocking script in `<head>` sets `data-fa-scheme` on `<html>` from the\n   reader's stored choice (`fa-color-scheme`, the key `docs-ui.js` writes),\n   else `prefers-color-scheme`, else **dark**. On the Jekyll site this is the\n   `fa-first-paint` block at the top of `_includes/head_custom.html`, and it\n   also switches the theme's stylesheet while the head is still being parsed,\n   so a light reader is light from the first frame too.\n2. **Paint `html` dark from the very first CSS** (light only when the\n   attribute says light). A page ground that nothing paints is the browser's\n   WHITE canvas whenever the theme's sheet is missing — a slow CDN, or a swap.\n3. **Never swap a stylesheet the page is already painting with.**\n   `jtd.setTheme(name)` swaps just-the-docs' first stylesheet, and a swap\n   UNLOADS the sheet until the new file arrives. Applying a stored \"dark\" on\n   this dark-configured site swapped `-default.css` for `-dark.css` — the same\n   colours — on every load: that was the white flash, for every reader who had\n   ever pressed the toggle. `applyScheme` in `docs-ui.js` now asks\n   `jtdShows(name)` first."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/theming/theme-artefacts.md#provenance-6",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "date",
      "cat-harness:section": "The page ground: the first paint is DARK",
      "prov:value": "**Pages that switch nothing with script cannot flash**, and do not need the\nsnippet: the generated dashboards (`state-visualizer.ts`,\n`gen-translation-status.ts`) paint dark from their first CSS, and the viewers\nthat follow `@media (prefers-color-scheme)` are decided by the browser before\nfirst paint. Do not give a dashboard the snippet as a tidy-up: it would switch\nON `data-fa-scheme=\"light\"` rules that were never finished (measured\n2026-09-24: 3–6 axe contrast failures per dashboard in light).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-24"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-24"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/theming/theme-artefacts.md#provenance-7",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "The mark: one geometry, two inks, and the pair is a MEASUREMENT",
      "prov:value": "Worked, from `cat-harness` on 2026-09-21 (bean `5r57`):",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 5r57",
        "2026-09-21"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-21"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/theming/theme-artefacts.md#provenance-8",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Absent is a real state",
      "prov:value": "An instance that declares no `mark-dark` renders its one mark in both\nschemes — what every instance did before the role existed. `imageForRole`\nreturns undefined and both templates fall back; nothing downstream\nspecial-cases a folio that never opted in."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/theming/theme-artefacts.md#provenance-9",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Tracing supplied art",
      "prov:value": "When the owner hands over a raster mark, trace it rather than approximating\nit by hand — the mark this replaced was a hand-drawn approximation that\ndiffered in kind from the original (a solid silhouette where the art was line\nwork). Three things that cost a cycle each here, worth knowing before the next\none:"
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/theming/theme-artefacts.md#provenance-10",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Tracing supplied art",
      "prov:value": "Check the reduction too, rather than assuming a small variant is needed: the\nold mark needed one because its whiskers were `stroke-width=\"2.4\"` on a 120\nviewBox, 0.32px at tab size. Fill-only art has no such floor, and the holes\nhere still survive at 16px (measured ink fraction 0.36, flat from 16 to 32)."
    }
  ]
